  "term": "brain plasticity",
  "definition": "Brain plasticity is the relative capacity of the brain and nervous system to be modified so that an individual can make new adjustments. In this historical source, it is presented as the basis of acquisition, especially learning and motor learning, and is contrasted with the fixed character of instinct and reflex action.",
